        <text class="d-ad" x="532" y="450">api-u3</text>
        <svg class="ico" x="502" y="466" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><use href="#i-globe"/></svg>
        <text class="d-ad" x="532" y="484">app-u3</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>Three branches up at the same time, on the daemon and the image cache you already have.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<style is:global>
/* The agent scene. A lane is grey until something in it is actually doing
   something, the same rule the walkthrough follows: a service that is not up
   is not coloured in. The colours are the CLI's own — amber for a universe,
   sky for an address, green for something running. */
#ag .ag-machine{fill:var(--raised);stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:2}
#ag .ag-card{fill:var(--raised);stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1.5}
#ag .ag-name{font:600 23px var(--sans);fill:var(--head)}
#ag .ag-stat{font:20px var(--mono);fill:var(--muted);transition:fill .3s}
#ag .ag-stat[data-ok="1"]{fill:var(--ok)}
#ag .ag-dot{fill:var(--muted)}
#ag .ag-wire{fill:none;stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:6 9}
#ag .ag-tok{fill:var(--num);opacity:0}
#ag .ag-req{fill:var(--addr);opacity:0}
#ag .ag-box{fill:none;stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:2;transition:stroke .4s}
#ag .ag-lane[data-live="1"] .ag-box{stroke:var(--num)}
#ag .ag-glow{fill:var(--num);fill-opacity:.07;stroke:none;opacity:0}
#ag .ag-svc,#ag .ag-net{color:var(--muted);transition:color .35s}
#ag .ag-svc[data-up="1"]{color:var(--ok)}
#ag .ag-net[data-up="1"]{color:var(--addr)}
#ag .ag-chip{fill:none;stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:1.5}
#ag .ag-lbl{font:20px var(--mono);fill:currentColor}
#ag .ag-adr{font:600 21px var(--mono);fill:currentColor}
#ag .ag-ok{fill:none;stroke:var(--ok);stroke-width:2.5;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;opacity:0}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  #ag .ag-stat,#ag .ag-box,#ag .ag-svc,#ag .ag-net{transition:none}
}
</style>
<section id="agents">
  <h2 id="agents"><a href="#agents">One universe per agent, on one machine</a></h2>
  <p>Give each coding agent a universe of its own and they work different branches, and different pull requests, at the same time &mdash; on the machine you already have. No second machine, no virtual machine, no cloud environment each: one Docker daemon, one image cache, one pool of CPU and memory, shared between them. It does not run the agents &mdash; it gives each one somewhere to run.</p>
  <figure class="fig wide" id="ag">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 720 500" role="img" aria-labelledby="gt gd">
      <title id="gt">Three coding agents on one machine, each committing to its own branch and checking its own running copy</title>
      <desc id="gd">One box labelled "your machine" holds three lanes side by side, one per agent: Claude on universe 1, branch feat/login; Codex on universe 2, branch fix/cart; OpenCode on universe 3, branch spike/redis. Each lane repeats the same cycle, staggered so all three are at a different point of it at once: the agent thinks, a commit travels down the wire into its universe, that universe's api, database and web services come up, its hostname answers, and 200 OK travels back up to the agent. Dashed walls stand between the lanes, because they share no network, no data and no ports. Along the bottom of the machine, a bar names what all three do share: one Docker daemon, one image cache, and the machine's CPU and memory.</desc>

