      <text class="d-m" x="260" y="466">one image cache</text>
      <svg class="ico" x="470" y="448" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><use href="#i-chip"/></svg>
      <text class="d-m" x="502" y="466">one CPU and RAM</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>All three at once, each on its own containers, its own data and its own hostnames &mdash; and none of them waiting for a port.</figcaption>
  </figure>


</section>

<section id="ready">
  <h2 id="ready"><a href="#ready">Agent-ready out of the box</a></h2>
  <p>No server and no protocol: an agent runs the command line, and one flag makes every command machine-readable &mdash; including its own help, so it can find its way without being told.</p>
  <div class="code"><pre><span class="p">$ </span>multiversectl --help --json          <span class="c"># every command and flag, as a document</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>multiversectl universe ls -o json    <span class="c"># the whole fleet, in few tokens</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>multiversectl agents skill install   <span class="c"># the skill, written for Claude Code</span></pre></div>
  <div class="cards">
    <a class="card" href="reference/cli.html">
      <strong><svg class="ico ci" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><use href="#i-code"/></svg>JSON on every command</strong>
      <span><code>--json</code> anywhere, <code>--less</code> for only what an agent must have.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="tasks/server.html#hw-agents">
      <strong><svg class="ico ci" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><use href="#i-bot"/></svg>A skill, installed for you</strong>
      <span>How to work in a universe of its own, and what never to do without asking.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card" href="tasks/catalog.html">
      <strong><svg class="ico ci" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 16 16"><use href="#i-doc"/></svg>An <code>AGENTS.md</code> of its own</strong>
      <span>Written into your multiverse's repository, saying what it is and how to run it.</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

